{{Horizontal Line}}


'''In other news'''
* A doorknob has been installed on the gong door in the God Wars Dungeon, allowing players inside the Bandos sector to click on the door to open it and leave. Previously, any player walking near that door would be teleported out whether they liked it or not; a simple doorknob renders this unnecessary.
* Items dropped in the Inferno now stay on the ground for 30 minutes before despawning.
* Teleports are no longer permitted inside the Inferno; there's no real need to teleport out of there, and players were triggering it by accident.
* Zaff's barrel of staffs, used to sell extra staffs to players who'd completed the Achievement Diaries, now appears differently based on whether you have already bought your ration for the day.

[[File:Pest Control & Open Weekend (7).png|center]]

'''Bugfixes'''

* The walls of the Monkey Madness II crash site cave no longer render over players and NPCs in the upper reaches of the cave.
* The bank now remembers its scroll position more reliably when closed and re-opened.
* The capitalisation of 'Lumbridge' has been corrected in a clue scroll.
* The code for fermenting wine has been optimised to better handle larger quantities of wine in your bank.
* The dragon scimitar ornament kit no longer has a graphical glitch when dropped on the ground.
* God swords no longer cause the serpentine helm to appear as though your head is detached.
* The Third Age robe top now renders more reliably over leg attire.

